|> Here are my questions:
|> 
|> 1) Do I really need 2 pets?  I now have both a large cat and a small
|> dog, it's kinda nice to have them help me but getting them downstais is
|> a pain.

Your pets probably won't last long.  If you want to get both of them
downstairs, and don't have a leash (or two) or a whistle, you may have
trouble getting them both to stand next to you while you go downstairs.
Here's a trick I sometimes use: Wait for one to stand next to you, and 
go downstairs.  Now come back without the first pet and wait for the 
second one to stand next to you.  As long as you aren't gone too long, 
they won't go wild on the level without you.
|> 
|> 2) I have a ring a levitation, can the monsters still attack me?  And
|> what kind of traps can I avoid?
|> 

Most monsters can still attack.
Not sure about traps -- probably pits, maybe bear traps.

|> 3) After praying once, I offered a couple of corpse to my altar, the
|> message were "The corpse disappears in flame" or something, what does
|> that suppose to mean?
|> 
You are in good standing with your god, but the great random number 
generator in the sky decided your sacrifice was not big enough to deserve
anything special.

|> 4) I also have a pick-axe, 2 magic markers (what are they good for?) and
|> a mirror, how should I use them.
|>

The pick-axe digs through walls, the floor, etc.  It's good for robbing
shops.
The mirror may scare monsters.  When you're blind and telepathic, and you
look at it, it tells you where the wizard is (Apply direction:".").
The magic markers may be used for writing scrolls on blank paper, or
writing Elbereth on the floor (scares monsters).
 
